course: dictionary
lesson: 1611
title: Cheetah: the fastest land animal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cheetah is a slim, spotted big cat, and it is the fastest land animal. When you meet a word you know only a little, read the words around it. «Spots tell them apart» means spots help you tell animals apart, so the spots are the clue that shows which cat is which.
explain: Context clues can also help with the word «tear» in «dark tear lines from eyes to mouth». Real tears are wet drops from the eyes, but the sentence says the lines run from the eyes to the mouth, so they are black markings on the face, not tears. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
explain: Before you trust a fact, check where it came from. The dictionary says cheetahs live in Africa and a few in Iran. «Most big cats hunt at night» is a fact about other big cats, and the cheetah is different because it hunts in the day.
fact: A cheetah is a slim, spotted big cat from Africa, and a few live in Iran.
fact: The cheetah is the fastest land animal. It can run as fast as a car on a main road, but only for a short burst.
fact: Cheetahs have black «tear lines» running from their eyes to their mouth.
fact: Cheetahs can purr but cannot roar, and they are endangered, which means they are at risk of dying out.
fact: «Cheetahs hunt in the day, while most big cats hunt at night.»
exercise: «The cheetah can run as fast as a car on a main road for a short burst.» What is the cheetah? | A slow, sleepy fish | A bird that cannot fly | *The fastest land animal | A kind of tree
exercise: Cheetahs can purr but cannot roar. What can the cheetah NOT do? | Hunt | Purr | *Roar | Run
exercise: «Cheetahs have dark tear lines from eyes to mouth.» What are tear lines? | Scratches from a fight | *Black lines on the face, from eyes to mouth | Real tears running down the face | Long stripes on the tail
test: «Cheetahs hunt gazelles in the daytime.» What is a gazelle? | A large, slow bird | *A slim, fast antelope | A small, spotted cat | A type of tree
test: Cheetahs are endangered. What does endangered mean? | Very large and strong | Happy and well fed | Able to fly | *At risk of dying out
exam: «Cheetahs hunt in the day, while most big cats hunt at night.» What does this tell us? | Most big cats hunt in the day | Cheetahs hunt only at night | *Cheetahs are different from most big cats, because they hunt in daylight | Cheetahs sleep all day
